; The smallest input that exercises E1's documented path: one parent and its
; point mutants, which is what `python -m E1.tools.score` takes as
; --parent-path plus --mutants-path. The first record is the parent; every
; record after it is a mutant of the same length.
;
; The sequences are the kit's own warm fixture, verbatim --
; e1/opt/e1_opt/tests/fixtures/warm/{parent,mutants}.fasta at commit
; f4f62fa6592ae4938d49b1757bea0cfeff9f468e: a 72-residue synthetic parent and
; five single-substitution mutants. Using the kit's fixture rather than a real
; protein means the smoke scores exactly what `bash run.sh warm` scores, so a
; difference between the two is a difference in this provider and not in the
; input.
